      "reason": "[\"The order appoints Admiral William D. Leahy Administrator of the Puerto Rico Reconstruction Administration and has him exercise the functions conferred by EO 7057, 7180 (as amended by 7554) and 7689; that tenure-bound grant ended when Leahy left office. The only held evidence is EO 8888 (dated 1941-09-03), which appoints Guy J. Swope \\\"vice Admiral William D. Leahy, resigned\\\", showing only that the resignation occurred between 1939-11-30 and 1941-09-03. The claim format requires an exact first-end date, and a not-later-than bound is not an exact end. EO 8888 does not name EO 8294. Missing source: Leahy's resignation or the acceptance of it as PRRA Administrator (agency or presidential record, or a Federal Register notice) giving its date. Whether to record the order as exhausted on issuance (1939-11-30) with the tenure as a surviving effect is a legal judgment this producer did not adopt, because the grant of functions is by its terms tied to his service.\"]"
